<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30154" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūtātor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				changer; an exchanger, barterer</i> (<b>poet.</b> and post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mutator circulus anni, i. e. Zodiacus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					10, 202</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mercis mutator Eoae, i. e. mercator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					854</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equorum, i. e. desultor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 6, 161</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mercium commerciorumque mutator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 3, 119</span></i>
			.</div>
